146. Among which, that which they seem most affraid of, is dispeopling the World and driving Folks into Monasteries, tho' I see none among us for them to run into were they ever so much inclin'd; but have heard it generally complain'd of by very good Protestants, that Monasteries were Abolish'd instead of being Reform'd;
